WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.448 --> 00:00:02.570
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.545
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:07.360
between Pizza Hut in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.203
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:14.900
In Japan, a Pizza Hut
pizza comes in three sizes.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.110
The smallest comes in a My Box order

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.563
and is approximately 15 centimeters.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.430
Our small can only be made
on a gluten-free crust.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.440
Check it out.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.460
Looks like something you would get

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.800
at your high-school cafeteria.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.620
And it measures 10 inches,
or 25.4 centimeters.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.036
Our next size up is a medium,

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.586
which is 26 centimeters.

00:00:40.003 --> 00:00:41.261
I'm gonna take this little guy.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.593
This pizza is so good, dude.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.738
And our large pizza is 14 inches,

00:00:51.738 --> 00:00:55.113
or 35.5 centimeters.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.670
This My Box pizza deal includes fries

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.160
and chicken nuggets for 1,080 yen,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.460
or add a Basque cheesecake

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.792
for 1,290 yen,

00:01:09.792 --> 00:01:12.976
or get three My Boxes

00:01:12.976 --> 00:01:15.484
for 3,000 yen,

00:01:15.484 --> 00:01:18.000
and you can get a free side menu item,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.540
like 1.5 liters of Coca-Cola.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.440
Also, for those wanting a little alcohol,

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.230
you can get a My Box deal

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:30.660
with an alcoholic beverage for 1,100 yen.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.355
It's called Being Tipsy set.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.271
Ah, tipsy.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.160
Now I'm going to the boxes, baby!

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.190
Our next size up is a $13 dinner box.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.340
It is a medium one-topping pizza,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.810
breadsticks, and cinnamon sticks.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.350
This is the best idea.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.475
If I had to go into an office,

00:01:52.475 --> 00:01:53.558
this would be my briefcase.

00:01:53.558 --> 00:01:55.870
This is what I would
take to work every day.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.100
Now, you're probably thinking,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.530
"Oh, Joe, I want more food in a box."

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.670
Well, Pizza Hut of course

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.340
has you covered with the big dinner box.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.006
Ah-hem.

00:02:05.006 --> 00:02:07.400
Oh, it is the big dinner box!

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.632
This is [grunts]

00:02:09.632 --> 00:02:12.620
two one-topping pizzas
with wings or breadsticks.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.550
That's what I got, of course.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.230
You can also get pasta and breadsticks.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.440
You can also get Quepapas and breadsticks,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.073
or just a third pizza,

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:22.250
all for $23.99 to $24.99.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.083
Man.

00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:24.949
Dinner is served.

00:02:24.949 --> 00:02:28.823
You can get chicken on
the bone in two pieces,

00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:31.630
four pieces, and eight pieces.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.930
That's really cute, Japan. Two wings.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.620
In the US, our wing orders start at six,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.453
12,

00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:39.286
18,

00:02:39.286 --> 00:02:41.778
and the biggest order you can get, 36.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.630
Wow, that's the hottest?

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.930
WingStreet, you gotta hire a spice expert,

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.556
because this is nothing, dude.

00:02:53.556 --> 00:02:55.633
I've had spicier LaCroixes.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.673
Here is a Japan large basic pizza.

00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:02.210
We call our cheese pizza basic,

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.920
and it is 2,030 yen.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.490
or $18.39 US.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.590
And it has a surface area of

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:15.156
754.77 square centimeters.

00:03:15.156 --> 00:03:18.454
So that is about $0.024,

00:03:18.454 --> 00:03:23.110
or 2.63 yen per square centimeter.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:26.240
The US large cheese pizza is $13.99,

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.150
or 1,544 Japanese yen.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.980
It has a surface area of
989.9 square centimeters,

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.121
which breaks down to $0.014

00:03:37.121 --> 00:03:39.254
per square centimeter,

00:03:39.254 --> 00:03:42.610
or 1.54 Japanese yen.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.910
Much cheaper here in the US.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.900
So, here are two large basic pizzas.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.920
This one right here is hand-tossed dough,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.700
and this one right here is a pan pizza.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.830
Here are two large US cheese pizzas.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.240
One of them has the pan crust,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.243
and one of them has the hand-tossed crust.

00:03:58.243 --> 00:04:01.610
Both are the same size and the same price.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.438
We want to find out which gives you

00:04:03.438 --> 00:04:06.160
more pizza for your money.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.100
Let's weigh a slice of each and compare.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:09.933
George: Go!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.618
So, winner is:

00:04:13.618 --> 00:04:15.684
ta-da!

00:04:15.684 --> 00:04:17.780
Hand-tossed dough.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:18.750
Oh, wow.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.633
That's, like,

00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:21.480
that's crazy, how good I did just there.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.521
Look at that.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.496
Same price, 25% more pizza.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:32.313
Look at these!

00:04:32.313 --> 00:04:34.423
Here's everything you can get

00:04:34.423 --> 00:04:38.210
at the Japanese Pizza Hut
you cannot get in the US.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.260
And here is everything you
can get at a US Pizza Hut

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.714
you can't get in Japan.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.356
Japan-exclusive pizzas!

00:04:44.356 --> 00:04:45.280
OK!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.910
So, I got everything on here

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.668
in half and half

00:04:49.668 --> 00:04:54.210
and in medium size on hand-tossed crust.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.260
All right, so let's start with this one.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.058
So I got this toku-uma bulgogi.

00:04:59.058 --> 00:05:01.965
Toku-uma means special delicious.

00:05:01.965 --> 00:05:05.040
So it's special delicious bulgogi.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.840
And this one is menta potemayo bacon.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.848
Menta means spicy cod roe,

00:05:11.848 --> 00:05:13.648
and it looks good.

00:05:13.648 --> 00:05:15.350
So, next one we've got

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:19.000
double shrimp with special lobster sauce,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.105
and this one is grand barbecue.

00:05:22.105 --> 00:05:23.740
Asparagus bacon.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.830
And this one is potato sausage mayo.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.410
Next one, we've got crumbling

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.380
pulled pork,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:36.200
and next one, spicy pulled pork.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.400
Selected cheese and thick-cut Iberico.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.880
And this one is Super Supreme.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.713
Mexican Kara Peno.

00:05:43.713 --> 00:05:45.779
Kara means it's spicy,

00:05:45.779 --> 00:05:48.395
so spicy jalapeño on there.

00:05:48.395 --> 00:05:52.207
And next one is snappy potato sausage.

00:05:52.207 --> 00:05:55.660
And this one is green
and yellow veggie pizza.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.320
Shrimp mayo mentai seafood.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.440
And this one is addictive
anchovy and black olive.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.391
First exclusive-US-pizza pizzas.

00:06:04.391 --> 00:06:07.016
This one right here, it
is the meat lover's pizza.

00:06:07.016 --> 00:06:08.070
Look at this thing!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.003
Can you see that?

00:06:09.003 --> 00:06:13.896
This thing is pepperoni,
Italian sausage, ham,

00:06:13.896 --> 00:06:16.993
bacon, seasoned pork, and beef.

00:06:16.993 --> 00:06:18.917
That's every meat in the store, I think.

00:06:18.917 --> 00:06:23.485
This one right here is the
Hawaiian chicken pizza.

00:06:23.485 --> 00:06:27.080
This looks like one bite
would send me to my grave.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.643
This at least has a vegetable on it.

00:06:31.248 --> 00:06:33.070
I think green peppers were a mistake.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.030
This one right here,

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.810
chicken bacon Parmesan.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:40.530
Chicken, bacon, tomatoes,
and a Parmesan crust.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.120
Oh, yeah, dude. Look at the crust on this.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.800
They bake the cheese right into the crust.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.563
I just love that Pizza Hut's like,

00:06:46.563 --> 00:06:48.821
"We gotta cover every
surface with cheese."

00:06:48.821 --> 00:06:50.780
God forbid you would take a bite

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.328
of something that doesn't
have cheese in it.

00:06:52.328 --> 00:06:54.164
In Japan, you can get a pizza

00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:56.618
with four different topping areas

00:06:56.618 --> 00:06:58.701
called the Four Series.

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:01.248
So let's start with this one.

00:07:01.248 --> 00:07:03.413
It's called Gochiso Four.

00:07:03.413 --> 00:07:05.323
Gochiso means feast.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:11.863
And next one, we've
got Bulgogi Festa Four.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.510
So, let's move on to the next one.

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.100
We've got Lovers Four.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.373
Lovers!

00:07:23.137 --> 00:07:24.310
What?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.000
Is this for this beef?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.125
It's gonna be horrible.

00:07:28.125 --> 00:07:31.540
And this one is called Kodawari Four.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.543
Kodawari means authentic.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.498
And this one in front of
me is Gourmet Mania Four.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.509
What did I do to you, Pizza Hut?

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:46.950
It's burned!

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.520
Look at this!

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.507
All right, next one.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.360
And the last one is Classic Four.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:56.526
This is classic.

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:00.460
Deluxe!

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.870
This one right here,

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.590
the backyard barbecue pizza.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.980
Barbecue sauce instead
of pizza sauce I think.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.960
And it comes with a
barbecue honey. Shall I?

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.381
I think I shall.

00:08:10.381 --> 00:08:12.415
Oh, yeah, I think I'm gonna like this.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.690
Don't sleep on the Pizza
Hut honey barbecue.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:17.690
This is really good.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:20.258
I think this is Buffalo chicken pizza.

00:08:20.258 --> 00:08:22.283
Tangy Buffalo sauce.

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.328
Exact opposite problem.

00:08:26.328 --> 00:08:27.303
I think the sauce ruins this.

00:08:27.303 --> 00:08:28.836
Too strong. Skip the sauce.

00:08:28.836 --> 00:08:32.780
So, this one right here
is a Japan-only pizza.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.121
So this is a pizza with a

00:08:35.121 --> 00:08:36.171
boom!

00:08:36.171 --> 00:08:37.701
Sausage crust

00:08:37.701 --> 00:08:41.008
with bulgogi, teriyaki chicken,

00:08:41.008 --> 00:08:45.360
Camembert cheese, Gouda
cheese, green chili sauce,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.510
shrimp, squid, tuna mayo,

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.718
broccoli, corn,

00:08:50.718 --> 00:08:53.930
basil sauce, and anchovies.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:54.870
Too much.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.435
But let's give it a try.

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:57.905
Look at this.

00:08:59.363 --> 00:09:00.919
Just too much.

00:09:00.919 --> 00:09:02.003
Itadakimasu.

00:09:05.145 --> 00:09:06.386
Mm.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.560
It's disgusting.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:13.210
In the first place, I hate anchovies.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.970
Don't put anchovies!

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:17.897
It's just

00:09:17.897 --> 00:09:18.830
mazui!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.440
I picked out that pizza for you, George.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.640
Sorry, my man. Gotta do it for the show.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.040
Here is a USA-only pizza.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.920
It is a pizza with toppings
and sauces and cheeses

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.050
you can only get in the
US and not in Japan.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.750
First, we have the gluten-free crust.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.903
Remember that really sad-looking crust?

00:09:32.903 --> 00:09:34.497
We can have a creamy garlic Parmesan,

00:09:34.497 --> 00:09:36.230
barbecue, or Buffalo sauce as a base.

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:38.355
I went with the creamy garlic Parmesan.

00:09:38.355 --> 00:09:41.105
Got meatballs, banana peppers,

00:09:41.105 --> 00:09:42.375
and for the crust,

00:09:42.375 --> 00:09:44.075
pretty sure I went the garlic Parmesan.

00:09:55.999 --> 00:09:57.510
It's not awful.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:59.900
When you order food and
you're, like, really hungry,

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.980
so something sounds like
it's gonna be really good,

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.080
but then when you start
eating it, you're like,

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.300
"Oh, I think I screwed up."

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:05.541
This is definitely like ...

00:10:05.541 --> 00:10:06.877
skip this.

00:10:06.877 --> 00:10:07.710
[thud]

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.060
So, here we've got
Japan's exclusive sides.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.926
We've got chicken nuggets,

00:10:12.926 --> 00:10:14.667
and this is four pieces,

00:10:14.667 --> 00:10:15.930
eight pieces,

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.180
16 pieces.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:20.720
And we also have plain
flavor and spicy flavor.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.810
Let's try this.

00:10:23.748 --> 00:10:25.886
Plain!

00:10:25.886 --> 00:10:27.800
This is plain.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.283
Everything is plain!

00:10:30.254 --> 00:10:31.287
I want spicy!

00:10:31.287 --> 00:10:33.810
Where is spicy nuggets?

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:37.210
And next one, we've
got honey cheese balls.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:41.310
So cheese balls there,
and we've got honey syrup.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:45.480
So, next one, we've got
Japanese-style tatsuta chicken.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:48.943
So this chicken is marinated in soy sauce

00:10:48.943 --> 00:10:52.601
and rolled in potato starch
instead of wheat flour

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:54.309
and deep-fried.

00:10:54.309 --> 00:10:56.610
Let's talk about US-exclusive sides.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.510
Can't get these in Japan.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.680
Pizza Hut also got pasta.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.370
Referred to at one point as Pasta Hut.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:06.190
You can get two of these baked
pastas at our Pizza Huts.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.134
One is the Tusca --

00:11:08.134 --> 00:11:09.042
Tuscani --

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:11.894
What? What'd I say?

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:14.083
Fine.

00:11:14.083 --> 00:11:16.330
No, Tuscany is T U S C A N Y.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.980
They spell this one with T U S C A N I.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.440
No, come on. I'm looking
it up. Keep rolling.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.430
Ad: Now at Pizza Hut,

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.378
get a family-size Tuscani pasta

00:11:25.378 --> 00:11:28.770
for just 12 bucks.
Joe: Ha-ha! Tuscani!

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.830
In your face!

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.890
Just an absolute abuse of Italian culture.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:36.840
Here is the Tuscani chicken Alfredo pasta

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.360
and the Tuscani meaty marinara pasta.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.370
If I can't put a fine enough point on it,

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.710
I do not want to eat this at all.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.070
This looks like a TV dinner.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.790
Like, this is what you
eat in your apartment

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.040
sitting on a folding chair,

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.540
one light bulb hanging from the ceiling,

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:49.920
eating this just right out of the oven,

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:50.920
staring at a wall,

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.000
looking at, like, cockroaches
running up and down.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.800
Your one window has a
view of a brick wall.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.770
The calendar on the wall
is from three years ago.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.140
♪ Nobody wants this! ♪

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:00.290
Quepapas.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.060
What are Quepapas, you ask?

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.030
I don't know.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:06.990
They got jalapeños and stuff in them.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.410
So they're kind of like spicy tater tots.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:13.040
These to me are quintessential
Pizza Hut sides.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.330
We got breadsticks, and
we got cheese sticks.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.000
They both come with the marinara sauce.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.050
We also have a marinara sauce
that you guys don't have.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.043
Vroom, vroom, vroom!

00:12:22.043 --> 00:12:23.580
Sauce Talk.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:26.690
So, here is extra sauces.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:27.800
So, if you want,

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.660
you can get green chili
sauce or honey syrup.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:34.230
So, the WingStreet wings
you can get at Pizza Hut

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.230
also come in exclusive flavors
you can't get in Japan.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.497
Here are all the sauces.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.030
Spicy garlic is really good.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.700
Joe's sauce seal of approval.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.470
Teriyaki, this seems like a no-brainer,

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.253
but we're not gonna leave it to chance.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:53.375
No!

00:12:53.375 --> 00:12:54.520
Ugh!

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.290
I stand corrected. This is terrible.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.360
Doesn't pass.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.630
Garlic Parmesan.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.080
Oh, look, there's Parmesan on top of it.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.468
Oh, yeah!

00:13:08.458 --> 00:13:09.960
That might be the best one.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:11.840
Lemon pepper dry rub.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.133
Why do I have to apply it?

00:13:18.022 --> 00:13:19.120
Yeah, not into that, man.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:19.953
I don't get it.

00:13:19.953 --> 00:13:21.143
I don't know what Drake's
going on about, man.

00:13:21.143 --> 00:13:22.210
The lemon pepper is not very good.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:23.500
Crucify me, internet!

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.630
I don't like lemon pepper dry rub wings!

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.230
Should I be -- I think maybe
I should be rubbing it,

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.392
that's what I'm doing wrong.

00:13:29.392 --> 00:13:30.634
Is that too much?

00:13:35.011 --> 00:13:35.844
Whoops.

00:13:35.844 --> 00:13:37.787
Yep, you were right. Too much.

00:13:37.787 --> 00:13:38.662
But it's good.

00:13:38.662 --> 00:13:40.180
Also, sauces, real quick,

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:41.510
we got blue cheese.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:42.935
We got ranch.

00:13:42.935 --> 00:13:46.210
So, here is Japan's exclusive desserts.

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:49.000
Here we've got Basque cheesecake.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:52.915
We've got Lady Borden vanilla ice cream.

00:13:52.915 --> 00:13:54.123
And last one,

00:13:54.123 --> 00:13:57.297
we've got Lady Borden chocolate ice cream.

00:13:57.297 --> 00:13:58.130
Desserts?

00:13:58.130 --> 00:13:58.963
We got 'em.

00:13:58.963 --> 00:14:01.018
In the US, you can get yourself this,

00:14:01.018 --> 00:14:04.540
a set of six Cinnabon cinnamon rolls.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:07.952
This is the triple-chocolate brownie.

00:14:07.952 --> 00:14:09.480
I'm starting to lose it, guys.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.140
All that pizza, it just hit me.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.710
This right here is the
ultimate chocolate chip cookie.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:14.730
This is pretty funny.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.200
They should cut this like a pizza.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.330
Cinnamon sticks.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.722
They also come with a thing of icing.

00:14:19.569 --> 00:14:21.298
Gonna be my obituary photo.

00:14:25.981 --> 00:14:27.610
I can't believe how good that is.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:28.443
This is the Cinnabon thing.

00:14:28.443 --> 00:14:29.920
I want to try it now,
since I had it before.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:30.966
I want to see how it compares to that.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.120
Cinnabon is still better.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:39.206
In Japan, our fountain drinks
are Coca-Cola products.

00:14:39.206 --> 00:14:41.640
In the US, our soft
drinks are Pepsi products.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.200
You know what that means.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.640
This is "Soda Wars."

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.630
In Japan, we have Coke,

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.110
Coke Zero,

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.740
and Fanta grape,

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.252
and green tea,

00:14:53.252 --> 00:14:55.133
and Qoo.

00:14:55.133 --> 00:14:56.560
Qoo orange juice.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:57.963
Look at this face.

00:15:03.496 --> 00:15:05.273
Qoo!

00:15:05.273 --> 00:15:08.490
It has light orange taste.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.430
Classic Pepsi,

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.540
cherry Pepsi,

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.920
diet Pepsi,

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:13.800
orange ...

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.050
Crush right? Yeah, Orange Crush.

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:15.883
Mountain Dew,

00:15:15.883 --> 00:15:17.670
and, of course, Sierra Mist.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.973
Which is like Mountain
Dew, only so much worse.

00:15:22.226 --> 00:15:23.059
[thud]

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:26.202
So, a full pizza

00:15:26.202 --> 00:15:29.752
is 2,256 calories.

00:15:29.752 --> 00:15:32.669
112.8%

00:15:32.669 --> 00:15:35.027
of your daily recommended value.

00:15:35.027 --> 00:15:36.968
Too many calories!

00:15:36.968 --> 00:15:38.259
Ah!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.878
In the US, our large cheese pan pizza

00:15:41.878 --> 00:15:42.711
has eight slices,

00:15:42.711 --> 00:15:44.900
and each slice is 360 calories.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:48.550
So for the total pizza,
that's 2,880 calories.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.730
That's 144% of your daily calories.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.360
And both the fat and the sodium

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.980
are each over 200% of
your daily allowance.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.713
Japan's large Pepperoni Supreme

00:15:58.713 --> 00:16:00.438
with plump bread crust

00:16:00.438 --> 00:16:03.680
is 228 calories per slice,

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:07.696
or 2,736 calories

00:16:07.696 --> 00:16:09.596
for the entire thing,

00:16:09.596 --> 00:16:13.237
which is 136.8%

00:16:13.237 --> 00:16:14.862
of your daily calories.

00:16:14.862 --> 00:16:16.763
Even more calories!

00:16:16.763 --> 00:16:18.804
Ah!

00:16:18.804 --> 00:16:22.333
This is a large US pepperoni
with the pan crust.

00:16:22.333 --> 00:16:24.010
Man, that's a thick guy!

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.290
One slice, 370 calories.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.935
So that makes the whole
pizza 2,930 calories,

00:16:29.935 --> 00:16:33.880
and that has 146.5% of
your daily allowance.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.670
Now, I would like to point out

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:37.328
that the large pepperoni pizza

00:16:37.328 --> 00:16:41.490
is the most popular Pizza
Hut pizza in the US,

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.222
but not in Japan.

00:16:43.222 --> 00:16:46.540
Online, it ranks about
the 14th most popular.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.840
In Japan, one of the pizzas we enjoy

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.780
is the seafood mix.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.630
It's one of Pizza Hut's best sellers

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:58.005
for over 20 years.

00:16:58.005 --> 00:16:58.950
Wow.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.262
So, Japan's most calorific pizza

00:17:01.262 --> 00:17:04.489
is the large toku-uma bulgogi.

00:17:04.489 --> 00:17:08.480
And I forgot to order
large toku-uma bulgogi!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:09.530
Sorry about that.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.730
But this one is toku-uma bulgogi.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:14.050
And this one is smaller,

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:18.660
but large slice pizza is 285 calories,

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:22.591
which makes the entire large
pizza on plump bread crust

00:17:22.591 --> 00:17:25.700
3,420 calories.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:29.161
3,420 calories!

00:17:31.343 --> 00:17:33.007
Yabai!

00:17:33.007 --> 00:17:33.840
And in the US,

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.260
our most calorific pizza
is the meat lover's.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.990
I also was supposed to get
the large. This is a medium.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:39.913
If someone in graphics

00:17:39.913 --> 00:17:41.496
could just make this pizza much bigger

00:17:41.496 --> 00:17:42.854
or me much smaller.

00:17:42.854 --> 00:17:46.651
One slice is 470 calories,
making the total pizza,

00:17:46.651 --> 00:17:48.309
which should be eight slices,

00:17:48.309 --> 00:17:50.667
3,760 calories.

00:17:50.667 --> 00:17:52.440
That's more than double your daily fat

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.909
and triple your daily sodium.

00:17:54.909 --> 00:17:56.610
I am a glutton for punishment,

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:58.230
but I'm not going to bite into this pizza.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.067
It looks like a nightmare.

00:18:01.974 --> 00:18:03.763
There's a few ingredients to watch out for

00:18:03.763 --> 00:18:05.320
at the Pizza Huts in the US.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:08.230
One is an ingredient found
in our salad croutons.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.204
It is called

00:18:09.204 --> 00:18:11.217
azodicarbonamidates.

00:18:11.217 --> 00:18:12.050
[beep]

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:12.883
Azo --

00:18:12.883 --> 00:18:13.716
[beep]

00:18:13.716 --> 00:18:15.880
Azodicarbonmidee.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:16.713
[beep]

00:18:16.713 --> 00:18:17.880
Or ADA.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.210
It is a substance used for making

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:21.480
vinyl foam plastics for
things like yoga mats.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.900
And it's also in our croutons.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:24.140
I'm not quite sure why.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.260
The use of this additive,

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.100
surprisingly enough,

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.490
is not permitted in Japan.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:28.490
What?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.517
That's just horrible!

00:18:30.517 --> 00:18:34.302
Both yoga mats and salads
have a connection to health.

00:18:34.302 --> 00:18:39.133
But US salad croutons
have actually plastic.

00:18:39.133 --> 00:18:40.990
Yoga-mat plastic.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.060
How ironic.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.100
Also in the US you're going
to want to watch out for

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.740
Yellow No. 5 aka tartrazine,

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.990
which appears in these
Cinnabon mini rolls.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.340
Oops, already ate one.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.850
According to the European Union,

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:55.233
this chemical, quote,

00:18:55.233 --> 00:18:57.150
"May have an adverse effect on activity

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.501
and attention in children," end quote.

00:18:59.501 --> 00:19:01.010
It is banned in the EU.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:02.510
It's not banned here in America.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.283
And it is at least not allowed

00:19:04.283 --> 00:19:06.057
at any of the Pizza Huts in Japan.

00:19:06.057 --> 00:19:08.282
You can totally get this here in America.

00:19:08.282 --> 00:19:11.321
Let's get some deficit on that attention.

00:19:11.321 --> 00:19:12.412
"May have adverse effect

00:19:12.412 --> 00:19:13.645
on activity and attention in children,"

00:19:13.645 --> 00:19:14.882
I mean, it's having a horrible effect

00:19:14.882 --> 00:19:16.565
on my attention as an adult.

00:19:16.565 --> 00:19:17.430
[laughs]

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:18.520
I stopped paying attention to

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.630
what was coming out of
my mouth moments ago. So.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.458
The Dew got Yellow No. 5 as well.

00:19:22.458 --> 00:19:26.672
The Orange Crush has Yellow
No. 6 and Red No. 40.

00:19:26.672 --> 00:19:28.400
Wonder if those are bad too.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.040
All the color things are bad.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.080
I have to say, this is also terrible.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:36.000
Why the hell American fast-food chains

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.815
put harmful chemicals into their foods?

00:19:39.815 --> 00:19:41.810
Do they make their food

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:44.496
in a chemistry laboratory or something?

00:19:44.496 --> 00:19:46.600
Use the kitchen.

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.770
Hey. If you're new to "Food Wars," hello.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.420
We actually have a whole nother series

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.060
where we compare the US and the UK.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.336
You can watch every one of
those episodes right now.

00:19:54.336 --> 00:19:56.123
Click the floating box near my head.

